  "question": "A short bar magnet placed with its axis at $30°$ to a uniform field of $0.25$ T experiences a torque of $4.5 \\times 10^{-2}$ N m. Find its magnetic moment in $\\text{A m}^2$.",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [],
  "answer": "",
  "numerical_answer": "0.36",
  "tolerance": "0",
  "solution": "$M = \\dfrac{\\tau}{B\\sin\\theta} = \\dfrac{4.5 \\times 10^{-2}}{0.25 \\times 0.5} = 0.36\\ \\text{A m}^2$.",
